{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And by what then shall it be known?</b> Even though they will enter the land and the angel will drive out the nations, by what shall it be known that this is a divine matter? For such is the way of all wars — one nation sometimes prevails over another and drives it out." "<b>Is it not in Your going with us, that we shall be distinguished?</b> As in: נָחִיתָ בְחַסְדְּךָ עַם זוּ גָּאָלְתָּ נֵהַלְתָ בְעָזְּךָ שָׁמְעוּ עַמִּים יִרְגָּזוּן (Exodus 15:13–14). For when the nations see that You are with us, we shall be in their eyes wondrous and distinguished in excellence above all other peoples, and they shall not be able to rise against us — as Rahab testified, saying: כִּי שָׁמַעְנוּ אֵת אֲשֶׁר הוֹבִישׁ ה׳ אֶת מֵי יַם סוּף, and וְלֹא קָמָה עוֹד רוּחַ בְּאִישׁ מִפְּנֵיכֶם, כִּי ה׳ אֱלֹהֵיכֶם הוּא אֱלֹהִים בַּשָּׁמַיִם מִמַּעַל וְעַל הָאָרֶץ מִתָּחַת (Joshua 2:10–11)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:01.007340168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}